Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["QSP phase gates: rotation angles for the qubit-controlled displacement circuit", "Title"],

Cell["This notebook compiles a phase gate exp(-i f(x)) on the oscillator position x into a sequence of qubit rotations interleaved with qubit-controlled displacements, using quantum signal processing (QSP). It is the compiler that produced the rotation angles run in the experiment for all five gates in the paper.", "Text"],

Cell["The steps are:", "Text"],

Cell["1. Expand exp(-i f(x)) in M+1 Fourier harmonics on the interval -2 <= x <= 2. Writing w = Exp[-I beta x], this gives a degree-M polynomial P(w) with coefficients co.", "Item"],

Cell["2. Find a complementary polynomial Q(w) such that |P|^2 + |Q|^2 = 1 for all |w| = 1, by numerical minimisation over the coefficients of Q.", "Item"],

Cell["3. Peel P and Q apart one layer at a time to get one rotation (theta, phi, lambda) per layer, and convert these angles to the echoed-conditional-displacement (ECD) convention used on hardware.", "Item"],

Cell["4. Rebuild the circuit from the angles and compare its P-block with the target.", "Item"],

Cell["The notebook is set up for the Morse gate. For the other gates change f and order in the first input cell; everything downstream is unchanged. Targets and orders used in the paper (f is the phase V(x) programmed by the gate):", "Text"],

Cell["cubic: f = 0.6 x^3, order = 11", "Item"],

Cell["symmetric double well: f = 0.1 x^4 - 0.3 x^2, order = 12", "Item"],

Cell["asymmetric double well: f = 0.1 x^4 - 0.3 x^2 + 0.1 x, order = 14", "Item"],

Cell["broken double well: f = 0.1 x^4 - 0.3 x^2 + 0.6 x, order = 13", "Item"],

Cell["Morse: f = 0.6 (1 - Exp[-0.8 (x + 0.5)])^2, order = 13", "Item"],

Cell["The multistart in Section 2 uses random seeds, so a rerun gives a Q (and hence angles) that can differ slightly from the stored outputs. The angles actually run are the stored outputs of Section 3 and are also listed in the Python operator-error notebook.", "Text"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["1. Target phase and its Fourier coefficients", "Section"],

Cell["xrange sets the Fourier interval -xrange <= x <= xrange, and beta = Pi/xrange is the displacement step, so w = Exp[-I beta x] is periodic on that interval. Here xrange = 2 and beta = Pi/2. order is the polynomial degree M (M+1 harmonics). f is the target phase.", "Text"],

Cell["co[[n+1]] is the n-th Fourier coefficient of exp(-i f(x)), computed by numerical integration over the interval. The extra factor Exp[-I order beta x/2] shifts the harmonics from -M/2..M/2 to 0..M so that they form an ordinary polynomial in w. exp is the resulting truncated series; it is the best the circuit can do at this order.", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"xrange", "=", "2"}], ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\[Beta]", "=", 
    RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "/", "xrange"}]}], ";"}], 
  RowBox[{"(*", 
   RowBox[{
   "range", " ", "of", " ", "x", " ", "with", " ", "good", " ", "accuracy"}], 
   "*)"}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"order", "=", " ", "13"}], ";", 
  RowBox[{"(*", 
   RowBox[{"order", " ", "of", " ", "polynomial"}], "*)"}], 
  "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{"f", "=", 
   RowBox[{"0.6", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"1", "-", 
       RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"-", "0.8"}], 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"x", "+", "0.5"}], ")"}]}], "]"}]}], ")"}], "^", "2"}]}]}], 
  ";", 
  RowBox[{"(*", 
   RowBox[{"set", " ", "the", " ", "potential"}], "*)"}], 
  "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{"co", "=", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"NIntegrate", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"-", "I"}], " ", "f"}], "]"}], "  ", 
          RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"-", "I"}], " ", "order", " ", "\[Beta]", " ", 
            RowBox[{"x", "/", "2"}]}], "]"}], 
          RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
           RowBox[{"I", " ", "n", " ", "\[Beta]", " ", "x"}], "]"}]}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"x", ",", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"-", "\[Pi]"}], "/", "\[Beta]"}], ",", 
           RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "/", "\[Beta]"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "/", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"2", 
         RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "/", "\[Beta]"}]}], ")"}]}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"n", ",", "0", ",", "order"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "//", 
    "Chop"}]}], ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"exp", "=", 
   RowBox[{"Sum", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"co", "\[LeftDoubleBracket]", 
       RowBox[{"n", "+", "1"}], "\[RightDoubleBracket]"}], 
      RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", "I"}], " ", "n", " ", "\[Beta]", " ", "x"}], "]"}]}], 
     ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"n", ",", "0", ",", "order"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
